>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In the ARP spoofing attack , the attacker can intercept the communication between network devices.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
500 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The attack works as follows:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
501 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The network must be accessible to the attacker. They search the network for the IP addresses of a minimum of two devices, assuming these are a router and a workstation. Here is the output of ARP table before the attack.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
502 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (arp -a)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
