/E (The MSSQL databases use the MS-TDS protocol over RPC. The RPC does not provide global relay protection or encryption. Depending on the configuration of the MSSQL client and server, the communication can be encrypted or plaintext. With encryption, another feature called Extended Protection is available since Windows 2018 R2 and Windows 7. Service Binding and Channel Binding can be enforced and protect against relaying attacks but this feature is disabled by default.)
